-- title:
--   Descent of mathcal O_D-homomorphisms along Pi, with Frobenius twist
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $B$ a Noetherian commutative ring. Let $X$ and $Y$ be formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules over $B$ in the sense of `FormalODModule`: each consists of a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law $F$ over $B$, a family `act` of pairs of power series indexed by $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$ and a further pair `varpi`, all of which are endomorphisms of $F$ in the sense of `IsLawHom` (constant coefficients zero, compatible with substitution into the group law), subject to $\mathrm{act}(1)=\mathrm{id}$, $\mathrm{act}(ab)=\mathrm{act}(a)\circ\mathrm{act}(b)$, $\mathrm{act}(a+b)=F(\mathrm{act}(a),\mathrm{act}(b))$, $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{varpi}=\mathrm{act}(p)$ and $\mathrm{varpi}\circ\mathrm{act}(a)=\mathrm{act}(\varphi(a))\circ\mathrm{varpi}$, where $\varphi$ is the Witt-vector Frobenius. Let $\psi$ be a pair of power series in two variables which is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from $X$ to $Y$, i.e. a homomorphism of laws $X.F\to Y.F$ commuting with all $\mathrm{act}(a)$ and with $\mathrm{varpi}$. Assume that $X.\mathrm{varpi}$ has kernel of degree $d$ for some $d$, meaning that $B[[x_1,x_2]]/(X.\mathrm{varpi}_1,X.\mathrm{varpi}_2)$ is a finite projective $B$-module whose base change along any ring homomorphism from $B$ to any field has dimension $d$; and assume each coordinate $\psi_i$ lies in the ideal generated by the coordinates of $X.\mathrm{varpi}$. Then there exists a pair of power series $\chi$ which is an $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphism from `frobTwist X` (the same law and same $\mathrm{varpi}$, with action $a\mapsto X.\mathrm{act}(\varphi(a))$) to $Y$ and satisfies $\chi\circ X.\mathrm{varpi}=\psi$ after substitution; moreover any pair $\chi'$ with vanishing constant coefficients and $\chi'\circ X.\mathrm{varpi}=\psi$ equals $\chi$, so uniqueness holds among all such $\chi'$, not merely among $\mathcal O_D$-homomorphisms.
--
--   This is isogeny descent along the isogeny $\Pi$ of a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module: a homomorphism vanishing on the finite locally free kernel of $\Pi$ factors through it, and the resulting factor is defined on the Frobenius twist of $X$ rather than on $X$ itself, the $\sigma$-semilinearity of $\Pi$ for the $\mathbb Z_{p^2}$-action becoming linearity out of the twist. It is used in the rigidification step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld description of fake elliptic curves, where it feeds the comparison of the relative Frobenius correspondence with the Atkin–Lehner quotient.
